WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390
Fire a beam of tiny, fast alpha
particles at a sheet of metal

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.890
foil, thinner than a hair.

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.410
Almost every one flies
straight through,

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.710
as if the foil were barely there.

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.790
But a very few bounce
almost straight back,

6
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.170
like a bullet off tissue paper.

7
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:21.610
Something inside those
atoms is pushing back, hard.

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.830
So what must the inside
of an atom be like?

9
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.510
In this mission, you'll
meet the protons,

10
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.510
neutrons and electrons
inside every atom.

11
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.450
You'll find out where an atom
keeps its mass and its charge,

12
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.050
and discover what makes two atoms
of the same element isotopes.

13
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.530
Your mission: work out what the
inside of an atom must be like.
